# Known false positives, so a REAL leak is visible.
#
# `gitleaks detect` exits non-zero whenever it finds anything, and this
# repository has always found the same four. That trains whoever runs it to
# read "leaks found: 4" as normal — which is precisely how a fifth, real one
# gets waved through. Each is recorded here with the reason it is not a
# credential, so the healthy state of this command is a clean exit.
#
# Fingerprint format is `commit:path:rule:startline`. It is pinned to the
# commit that introduced the line, so editing the file later does NOT silently
# keep the exemption alive — a genuinely new secret on the same line is a new
# fingerprint and will be reported.
#
# Verified independently on PC1 and PC2, 8–9 August 2026
# (docs/DAY12_SECURITY_PASS.md §5).

